    "full_rank_observation_operator_requirement": "Exact step re-initialization (x = x_minus + H^{-1} y, P = H^{-1} R H^{-T}) requires full-rank observation matrix H (rank=dim(x)=6). When fewer than 3 independent spatial-temporal medoid projections are observable, H becomes rank-deficient, and the tracker must remain in 'pending_impulse' or fall back to pseudo-inverse regularized estimation.",
    "threshold_hugging_ambiguity_regime": "Innovations in the near-boundary interval [3.8 sigma, 4.2 sigma] exhibit transient classification ambiguity on frame t. The 1-sample causal deferral gate handles this honestly: it holds belief at frame t, and resolves ambiguity at frame t+1 via the persistence check (confirming maneuver vs rejecting glint).",
    "causal_action_ratio_boundary": "Active Causal Generators (G_act) and Driven Passive Registers (Omega_reg) are partitioned at eta_nonlocal = 0.50. Swarms with high feedback coupling in eta in [0.45, 0.55] require 4-frame temporal smoothing of eta_nonlocal to prevent flicker.",
    "mass_continuity_dissipation_limit": "TemporalClockContentSplitter assumes moving target conservation (sigma_c = 0). Targets undergoing rapid aspect-ratio expansion or total thermal bloom dissipation produce non-zero sigma_c and are partitioned through the irreversible clutter channel."
